WEBVTT

00:00:56.537 --> 00:01:00.121
If they destroy the corrupted one, 
the malware will be defeated.

00:01:00.121 --> 00:01:03.829
Any others, and the virus will erase 
the entire system.

00:01:04.413 --> 00:01:07.121
The lights are only visible 
within the mainframe,

00:01:07.121 --> 00:01:11.246
so you won’t know until you get there 
which, if any, are on.

00:01:11.621 --> 00:01:14.871
How can you communicate, 
with your single action,

00:01:14.871 --> 00:01:17.454
which of the 4 disks
has been corrupted?

00:01:17.454 --> 00:01:20.163
Pause here to figure it out for yourself.
Answer in 3

00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:22.663
Answer in 2

00:01:22.663 --> 00:01:25.246
Answer in 1

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:28.579
The setting is a big clue 
for one solution.

00:01:28.579 --> 00:01:34.246
Using binary code— the base two 
numbering system that only uses 1s and 0s—